---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Feedback">
	<p>
		After each weekend, we ask you to complete a short survey about your
		experience. This really helps us understand what's working well, and
		what we can improve for next time, so please fill it in!
	</p>
	<p><a href="https://tally.so/r/ja7vEY">Feedback form for April 2026</a></p>
	<h2>Feedback from the last event</h2>
	<h3>Overall Feedback: Excellent!</h3>
	<p>
		You consistently tell us that the range of workshops, quality of
		teaching and the weekend as a whole are excellent! This is amazing for a
		community-driven, co-operative event like BIP and means we prefer
		cautious experiments to sweeping changes.
	</p>
	<h3>The longer event</h3>
	<p
		>Most people enjoyed having a longer event, but for contradictory
		reasons! Some enjoyed having more time to relax and socialise, while
		others said it was more intense, and others were disappointed that there
		weren't more workshops.</p
	><p
		>Several people asked about having another long event, but many people
		were concerned that the additional time off required would make it
		impossible for them to attend regularly.</p
	><p
		>While we're not ruling out organising another extra-long event in the
		future, we need to think carefully about what audience we want to serve
		with a longer event. For the forseeable, we'll be sticking to the
		Friday–Sunday timings.</p
	>
	<h3>Programme & The App</h3>
	<p>
		The biggest area for developmental feedback was about how we share the
		event schedule with you. Alex has made numerous changes and improvements
		to this app:
		<ul>
			<li
				>You can now <a href="/workshops"
					>see all the workshops for the weekend on one page</a
				></li
			>
			<li>The menu is easier to navigate and close</li>
			<li
				>It takes fewer clicks to set your favourites for each session</li
			>
			<li>The timings of each event are displayed more clearly</li>
			<li>There's more detail about the evening entertainment again</li>
		</ul>
		Several people also requested the return of the PDF version. Arranging all
		the details into a 40-page document is hugely time-consuming, and our feedback
		suggests that only a small fraction of people actually use it except for the
		timetable at the back. In the interests of getting the programme to you quicker
		(and being able to make adjustments more quickly when things change) we won't
		be bringing back the full PDF programme. However, we have produced a one-page
		timetable that you can print out if you prefer a paper version.
	</p>
	<h3>Other Activities</h3>
	<p>
		Last time we took advantage of the longer event to run events to promote
		community, networking and knowledge-sharing: Improv Speed Dating and Ask
		the Expert.</p
	>
	<p
		>Both events were reasonably well received, but Ask the Expert had
		limited attendees. Most people really enjoyed Improv Speed Dating, but a
		few people had strongly negative experiences where their partners pushed
		the conversation in an unwelcome direction. We're giving these a break
		for this event and will be looking at other ways to encourage making new
		friends at future events.
	</p>
</Layout>
